            <div xml:id="d1024">

                <pb facs="0954" n="640" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg640"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/796</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Vice Consul at
                        Valparaiso</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Easterling</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-28T17:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 28, 1914. 5 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Yours November 26, 4 p. [<hi rendition="#italic">a.</hi>] m. and 9 p.m.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d1024-f1"/> Report amounts and kinds of cargo supplied to
                    German vessels at sea and names of such vessels. Cable briefly other
                    irregularities known. Investigate thoroughly but discreetly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
